alex (devex): Heads up — after publishing @home/sdks-js v2.1.0 the edge samples (Deno / Cloudflare Workers) started failing with import errors: "package exports not found".

maria (sdk): oh no. did we change package.json exports in the build? any repro steps?

sam (build): repro on my laptop: node 18 import works, Deno fails. esbuild-based bundler also errors with unresolved entry. stack trace snippet: 
Error: Cannot find module '.../node_modules/@home/sdks-js'

kevin (eng): here's the minimal exports block we shipped:
{
  "exports": {
    ".": {
      "import": "./dist/index.mjs",
      "require": "./dist/index.cjs"
    }
  }
}

maria (sdk): okay — that's valid for node import/require, but Deno and many edge runtimes don't honour node conditional exports and often need an unconditional ESM path or a plain entry file. also TS projects can break if the `types` field doesn't point at dist/index.d.ts.

sam (build): quick workaround for affected customers: `import sdk from "@home/sdks-js/dist/index.mjs"` — but messy. we should ship a compatibility export.

alex (devex): thinking we should add a fallback export and a `worker` condition. something like:
{
  "exports": {
    ".": {
      "import": "./dist/index.mjs",
      "require": "./dist/index.cjs",
      "worker": "./dist/index.mjs",
      "default": "./dist/index.mjs"
    }
  },
  "types": "./dist/index.d.ts"
}

maria (sdk): will prepare a patch. proposed plan: 1) add unconditional ESM fallback and `worker` condition; 2) ensure `types` points to built d.ts; 3) emit both .mjs and .cjs artifacts in dist; 4) add a tiny migration note in changelog and sample edge snippet.

ci-bot: build #4721 failed on deno-lint in samples/edge after upgrade.

kevin (eng): also add a short sample in samples/edge that imports from the top-level and one that imports the dist path so consumers can see both patterns. will help support triage.

alex (devex): cool. assigning to @maria as a release-blocker for the SDK. we should also add a one-line note in onboarding guide about export map quirks and edge runtimes. :+1:
